---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const shows = [
  "Closures and crashes",
  "Road conditions reported by snowplows",
  "Weather alerts along your route",
];
---

<BaseLayout description="TravelDot checks your Minnesota route for closures, crashes, plow-reported road conditions and weather alerts before you leave.">
  <h1>Know your road before you go.</h1>
  <p>
    Enter where you're starting and where you're headed. TravelDot checks every stretch of the route
    against live road reports and current weather, then tells you what's on your road in plain
    language.
  </p>

  <h2>What it shows</h2>
  <ul>
    {shows.map((item) => (
      <li>{item}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>When you're ready to leave, one tap opens the trip in your navigation app.</p>

  <h2>Starting with Minnesota</h2>
  <p>
    TravelDot launches in Minnesota and covers the state's interstates, US highways and state
    highways. County and city roads aren't included. Other states that publish 511 road data may
    come next.
  </p>

  <h2 id="waitlist">Coming to iPhone and Android</h2>
  <p>Join the waitlist and we'll email you when it's out.</p>
</BaseLayout>
